Subject: register VM I2 verify scans live values once per boundary

What this does:
  The I2 promoted-slot check at block boundaries walked every live value once
  per promoted slot. It now makes a single pass over the live values per
  boundary, recording the value seen for each slot in `seen`, then checks each
  slot's expected value.

Why we need it:
  The per-slot walk made this verification quadratic in the frame size.

Needs a bytecode version bump:
  No. Lowering only.

